{"E:\\videos\\olc02\\wt\\vlog\\olc04\\voz\\b004_t5.wav": {"text": "A one-pound bag of dry pinnos at the store is about $1.80. Cooked, it makes about six cups. A can of beans, one and a half cups, is about a dollar and a quarter. So the bag gives you four cans worth of beans for the price of a can and a half. Cook a bag every week for a year and that's hundreds of dollars left in your pocket from one thing. Now the pot. Part one is picking. Pour your beans out on a sheet pan and look at them. You'll find little stones, a cloud of dirt, a few shriveled or broken beans. Pick them out. In the camp, the cookie did this every morning. And once Lars found a stone the size of a pea that would have broken somebody's tooth. Then wrenched them in a colander. And now here's the thing everybody argues about. You do not need to soak them overnight. Soaking saves you 20 or 30 minutes of simmer, that's all. If you forgot to soak them, you lost nothing.", "words": [{"w": " A", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.26}, {"w": " one-pound", "s": 0.26, "e": 0.74}, {"w": " bag", "s": 0.74, "e": 1.1}, {"w": " of", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.32}, {"w": " dry", "s": 1.32, "e": 1.68}, {"w": " pinnos", "s": 1.68, "e": 2.0}, {"w": " at", "s": 2.0, "e": 2.26}, {"w": " the", "s": 2.26, "e": 2.48}, {"w": " store", "s": 2.48, "e": 2.7}, {"w": " is", "s": 2.7, "e": 2.9}, {"w": " about $1.80.", "s": 2.9, "e": 4.5}, {"w": " Cooked,", "s": 4.5, "e": 4.84}, {"w": " it", "s": 4.84, "e": 4.94}, {"w": " makes", "s": 4.94, "e": 5.22}, {"w": " about", "s": 5.22, "e": 5.6}, {"w": " six", "s": 5.6, "e": 5.94}, {"w": " cups.", "s": 5.94, "e": 6.62}, {"w": " A", "s": 6.64, "e": 6.78}, {"w": " can", "s": 6.78, "e": 6.98}, {"w": " of", "s": 6.98, "e": 7.22}, {"w": " beans,", "s": 7.22, "e": 7.7}, {"w": " one", "s": 7.7, "e": 7.84}, {"w": " and", "s": 7.84, "e": 7.94}, {"w": " a", "s": 7.94, "e": 8.08}, {"w": " half", "s": 8.08, "e": 8.3}, {"w": " cups,", "s": 8.3, "e": 9.02}, {"w": " is", "s": 9.02, "e": 9.14}, {"w": " about", "s": 9.14, "e":